WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.539
Film Courage: Can we talk about core formats
and that’s a term that is new for me.

00:00:03.539 --> 00:00:07.879
So what should a writer know about creating
story for each one and I understand in your

00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:11.830
book [STORY MAPS: How To Write A GREAT Screenplay]
you talk about the 1-hour drama or dreamed,

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:18.910
30 minute single-camera sitcom, 30-minute
multi-camera sitcom, a 30-minute dramedy hybrid

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.700
or web series which is incredibly popular.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:27.070
Daniel Calvisi: Well first things first, write
something that you would want to watch.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:34.120
Write a format that you love, that you would
want to watch so if you prefer one-hour dramas

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:40.140
like Breaking Bad, Mad Men or something like
that, then write one of those ideally you

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.079
would know those formats.

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:48.840
So if you love Breaking Bad, Mad Men, The
Good Wife then you would probably know a little

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.019
bit more about that format.

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:53.980
You’ve just internalized a little bit more
about that format and ideally you want to

00:00:53.980 --> 00:01:00.699
map out or outline out several episodes of
your favorite shows before you tackle that

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:02.479
first pilot.

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:07.610
So you understand the structure a little bit
more and you’re not just writing freeform,

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:11.340
especially if you are coming from features
because you really need to understand the

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.830
TV structure.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:16.910
So write what you know and love and would
watch.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:21.750
The 30-minute dramedy, they tend to have more
of a cultural viewpoint.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:28.240
There’s more diversity in the 30-minute
dramedies and they’re more set in a specific

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:34.930
world definitely more than like a multi-camera
sitcom like the Big Bang Theory for example.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:40.410
It’s more of a subculture, it’s more of
a micro-culture and I guess you’d say a

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.920
personal viewpoint.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.480
But the more personal you can get, the more
specific you can get that applies to any format.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.990
Film Courage: What do you see many people
venturing into these days, like the web series

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:52.990
space?

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.960
What has been the most popular in 2016-2017?

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:03.300
Daniel Calvisi: Well, there are more 1-hour
scripted dramas than other formats.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:10.180
Actually out there in the marketplace like
on cable, on your TV, or on a streaming service

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.810
like Amazon or Netflix, so there are more
of those.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:17.540
But I really think you should write what you
want to watch.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.420
So it’s really up to you.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:24.530
There may be more 1-hours being made than
any other format but in my opinion the most

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:32.569
interesting and unique and experimental form
is the 30-minute single camera show, whether

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:38.770
it’s a single camera sitcom or a single
camera dramedy hybrid, there is just more

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:39.770
going on there.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:46.569
There is more unique, creator driven than
ever in that format and I would like to think

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:51.780
that networks are more open to it and streaming
services are more open to it because it is

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:58.000
cheaper to create, to produce a 30-minute
show than a 1-hour scripted show, certainly

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.319
like a 1-hour action show or a 1-hour period
piece.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:04.180
Those are going to be really expensive.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:09.730
So it’s cheaper and some of them come from
web series, something like Issa Rae Insecure

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:12.349
started as a web series.

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:14.959
Difficult People was a web series.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:39.989
So it’s easier to get in the door with an
established 30-minute series.

